Debian Package Building Instructions
====================================

This directory contains the Debian packaging files for OLLMchat.

Packaging modes
---------------

Three layouts are maintained. The **split** layout is the default in git and
what CI publishes to the [roojs APT repository](https://roojs.github.io/repos/).

### Split packages (default)

Builds separate runtime libraries, matching `-dev` packages, the application,
tools, and examples. This is the layout other applications use to depend on
`libocrpc-dev` (and the other libraries) without installing the whole app.

```bash
# libllama-dev from https://roojs.github.io/repos/ (CI: scripts/ci/enable-roojs-apt.sh)
./debian/use-split-packages.sh   # already the default in git
dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b
```

### Monolithic (optional all-in-one)

Single `ollmchat` `.deb` that bundles the application, shared libraries, GIR
data, and command-line tools (local GGUF via libllama).

```bash
./debian/use-monolithic-package.sh
dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b
./debian/use-split-packages.sh   # switch back when done
```

### Remote-only (all-in-one, no libllama)

Single `ollmchat-remote-only` `.deb` built with `-Dlocal_gguf=disabled`. It
conflicts with `ollmchat` and with the split library packages (they cannot
share `/usr/lib/*/libocrpc.so`).

```bash
./debian/use-monolithic-remote-only-package.sh
dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b
./debian/use-split-packages.sh   # switch back when done
```

`ollmchat` and `ollmchat-remote-only` conflict; only one may be installed at
a time. Both install the same `/usr/bin/ollmchat` application.

The active variant is selected by the switch script, which copies the matching
`control`, `.install`, and `not-installed` files and writes `debian/local-gguf`
(`enabled` or `disabled`). `debian/rules` passes that to Meson as
`-Dlocal_gguf=…`.

Canonical definitions live in `debian/split/`, `debian/monolithic/`, and
`debian/monolithic-remote-only/`.

GitHub release AppImages and the Windows installer use a **remote-only**
build (no libllama). See `docs/creating-releases.md`.

Split package layout
--------------------

When using split packages, the source builds:

### Core / data libraries
1. **libocsqlite1** / **libocsqlite-dev** — SQLite helpers (libocsqlite.so)
2. **libocrpc1** / **libocrpc-dev** — Binary RPC wire types (libocrpc.so)
3. **libocfiles1** / **libocfiles-dev** — File and project management (libocfiles.so)
4. **libollamaweb1** / **libollamaweb-dev** — Ollama HTTP client (libollamaweb.so)
5. **libochf1** / **libochf-dev** — Hugging Face Hub catalog (libochf.so)

### Markdown libraries
6. **libocmarkdown1** / **libocmarkdown-dev** — Markdown parsing (libocmarkdown.so)
7. **libocmarkdowngtk1** / **libocmarkdowngtk-dev** — GTK markdown rendering (libocmarkdowngtk.so)

### LLM stack libraries
8. **libollmchat1** / **libollmchat-dev** — LLM API access (libollmchat.so)
9. **libollmchatgtk1** / **libollmchatgtk-dev** — GTK chat widgets (libollmchatgtk.so)
10. **liboctools1** / **liboctools-dev** — LLM tool implementations (liboctools.so)
11. **libocvector2-1** / **libocvector2-dev** — Daemon FAISS vector search (libocvector2.so)
12. **liboccoder1** / **liboccoder-dev** — Code editor / agent UI (liboccoder.so)
13. **libocmcp1** / **libocmcp-dev** — MCP integration (libocmcp.so)
14. **libocwebkit1** / **libocwebkit-dev** — WebKitGTK browser tool (libocwebkit.so)
15. **libocbwrap1** / **libocbwrap-dev** — bubblewrap / seccomp helpers (libocbwrap.so)

### Application and tools
16. **ollmchat** — Main application and ollmfilesd daemon
17. **ollmchat-tools** — Command-line tools (oc-md2html, oc-html2md)
18. **ollmchat-doc** — Example and test executables

To reuse the RPC library from another Vala project:

```bash
sudo apt-get install libocrpc-dev
```

That pulls in `libocrpc1` plus the GLib / Gee / JSON-GLib / libsoup development
packages. The VAPI is `/usr/share/vala/vapi/ocrpc.vapi`.

Building packages
-----------------

1. Install build dependencies on Debian 13 or Ubuntu 25.04+ (add the [roojs APT source](https://roojs.github.io/repos/) first so `libllama-dev` resolves; GitHub Actions uses `scripts/ci/enable-roojs-apt.sh`):
   ```bash
   sudo apt-get install build-essential devscripts debhelper meson ninja-build \
     pkg-config valac libgee-0.8-dev libglib2.0-dev libjson-glib-dev \
     libsoup-3.0-dev libxml2-dev libsqlite3-dev \
     libgtk-4-dev libgtksourceview-5-dev libadwaita-1-dev libsecret-1-dev \
     libwebkitgtk-6.0-dev libwebkitgtk-6.0-webdriver-dev libatspi2.0-dev gobject-introspection \
     libgirepository1.0-dev libtree-sitter-dev libseccomp-dev libgit2-glib-1.0-dev \
     libopenblas-dev liblapack-dev libfaiss-dev libllama-dev
   ```

2. Build the packages:
   ```bash
   dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b
   ```

3. The resulting .deb files will be in the parent directory.

Install locations
-----------------

- Libraries: /usr/lib/
- VAPI files: /usr/share/vala/vapi/ (`*-dev` packages)
- GIR files: /usr/share/gir-1.0/ (`*-dev` packages, where generated)
- Typelib files: /usr/lib/*/girepository-1.0/ (runtime library packages)
- Application: /usr/bin/ (ollmchat)
- Tools: /usr/bin/ (oc-md2html, oc-html2md)
- Test executables: /usr/bin/ and /usr/share/doc/ollmchat/ (ollmchat-doc)

Vala consumers of `libocrpc-dev` pick up `/usr/share/vala/vapi/ocrpc.vapi` automatically.
